From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Fri, 25 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rw-system: disable OPPO touch firmware update on MT6771 to
 prevent kernel panic

The OPPO F11 (CPH1911, MT6771/Helio P70) bootloops because the
touchscreen driver (td4320_nf) triggers a kernel panic during
firmware change. After the panic, the MediaTek watchdog (toprgu)
triggers a hard reset, causing a bootloop.

This is a kernel-space issue that occurs before userspace runs.
However, the td4320_nf driver reads a firmware update flag from
a sysfs node that can be controlled by the vendor. Some OPPO
devices expose /proc/touchpanel/fw_update or similar proc entries
that control whether the touch driver performs a firmware update
on boot.

For OPPO/Realme MediaTek devices, write 0 to any known touch
firmware update sysfs/proc nodes during rw-system.sh (post-fs)
to prevent the driver from attempting a firmware change that
could cause a kernel panic. This is a best-effort mitigation —
if the driver doesn't expose such a node, or the panic occurs
before post-fs, this will have no effect.

Issue: #45
---
 rw-system.sh | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rw-system.sh b/rw-system.sh
index c3d8f5e..e4f2a1b 100644
--- a/rw-system.sh
+++ b/rw-system.sh
@@ -378,6 +378,18 @@ for part in /dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/oppodycnvbk  /dev/block/platform/bootd
         setprop ro.build.overlay.deviceid "$oppoName"
     fi
 done
+
+# Disable touch firmware update on OPPO/Realme MTK devices to prevent
+# kernel panic from td4320_nf driver during boot. The driver triggers
+# a kernel panic during firmware change on some devices (notably OPPO F11
+# CPH1911 MT6771). Writing 0 to the firmware update flag prevents the
+# driver from attempting the update.
+for node in /proc/touchpanel/fw_update /sys/devices/platform/tpd/fw_update /proc/tfa98xx/oppo_tfa98xx_fw_update; do
+    if [ -f "$node" ]; then
+        echo 0 > "$node" 2>/dev/null
+        log -t rw-system "Disabled touch fw update at $node"
+    fi
+done
 
 if ! getprop ro.product.vendor.model | grep -q -e oppo6771; then
 
-- 
2.53.0